urns\r\n4. Diabetes mellitus\r\n5. Pressure and tissue ischemia\r\n6. Frostbite\r\n\r\nTypes of Gangrene\r\n\r\n1. Dry gangrene\r\n\r\n* Usually caused by progressive loss of arterial blood supply.\r\n* Tissue becomes dry, shriveled and black.\r\n* Usually develops slowly.\r\n* There is a clear line of demarcation between healthy and dead tissue.\r\n* Infection is initially minimal.\r\n\r\n2. Wet gangrene\r\n\r\n* Occurs when ischemic tissue becomes infected.\r\n* Tissue is swollen, soft and discolored.\r\n* Pus and foul-smelling discharge may be present.\r\n* Spreads rapidly.\r\n* Can lead to sepsi\n<truncated 2504 bytes>\n3. Investigations for Musculoskeletal Disorders BPT 3rd Year Physiotherapy | Easy-language university exam notes | 10-mark answers Reference: David J. Magee, Orthopedic Physical Assessment (assessment principles). Simplified study notes; not verbatim textbook content. Contents • 1. Blood Investigations and Markers • 2. Ultrasonography (USG) • 3. X-ray (Radiography) • 4. Computed Tomography (CT Scan) • 5. Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) Page 1 BPT Physiotherapy Study Notes1. Blood Investigations and Markers Definition: Blood investigations are laboratory tests performed on a blood sample to detect inflammation, infection, autoimmune disease, muscle injury, and metabolic problems affecting bones and joints. In simple words: Blood tests help identify whether a musculoskeletal problem may be due to infection, inflammation, an immune disorder, or a metabolic problem. Aims • Detect infection and inflammation. • Identify autoimmune diseases such as rheumatoid arthritis. • Assess bone and mineral met\n<truncated 10746 bytes>\n4. I removed these lines because I copied them from the pdf : BPT Physiotherapy Study Notes    and all page x -      so start your work : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------        Investigations for Musculoskeletal Disorders BPT 3rd Year Physiotherapy | Easy-language u